00:47:57,830 --> 00:48:03,750
Stamina's looking good too. Speed is nice — max speed hits 56.9.

826
00:48:03,750 --> 00:48:10,580
Strong.

827
00:48:10,580 --> 00:48:16,420
Let's paint the car! You can't do it on cars, sadly.

828
00:48:16,700 --> 00:48:21,220
That's a shame

829
00:48:21,220 --> 00:48:32,620
Let's mess around with graffiti

830
00:48:32,620 --> 00:48:38,320
Wow, it's starting to feel like a rough neighborhood

831
00:48:38,320 --> 00:48:39,360
Okay

832
00:48:39,360 --> 00:48:41,880
Okay

833
00:48:41,880 --> 00:48:45,300
Looks safe here

834
00:48:45,300 --> 00:48:51,840
Hmm, what should I do

835
00:48:51,840 --> 00:48:54,500
What day is it today?

836
00:48:54,500 --> 00:48:56,920
August

837
00:48:56,920 --> 00:49:06,950
Hey! Graffiti is blocked here

838
00:49:06,950 --> 00:49:08,930
Did a dome go up?

839
00:49:08,930 --> 00:49:12,170
I wonder where

840
00:49:12,170 --> 00:49:15,490
Koyori!

841
00:49:15,490 --> 00:49:16,570
Koyori!

842
00:49:16,570 --> 00:49:18,610
Yoohoo!

843
00:49:18,610 --> 00:49:21,330
Polka-senpai!

844
00:49:21,330 --> 00:49:22,110
What's up?

845
00:49:22,110 --> 00:49:24,210
So flashy!

846
00:49:24,210 --> 00:49:26,090
That's totally Polka-senpai's colors!

847
00:49:26,090 --> 00:49:29,430
Today I'm wearing a jacket over my pajamas

848
00:49:29,430 --> 00:49:31,430
Today I was thinking of going by car

849
00:49:31,430 --> 00:49:33,430
Yeah that does look pajama-ish

850
00:49:33,430 --> 00:49:35,230
Wait, seriously? That's awesome!

851
00:49:35,230 --> 00:49:37,030
A camper van, I'm so happy

852
00:49:37,030 --> 00:49:40,630
Look look look — it's scary, the rack floated

853
00:49:40,630 --> 00:49:42,430
Where where where?

854
00:49:42,430 --> 00:49:46,030
Wait, no way? It disappeared from the rack floating?

855
00:49:46,030 --> 00:49:47,630
No way?

856
00:49:47,630 --> 00:49:51,430
This is the kind of thing that gets you arrested — if you had 3 days

857
00:49:51,430 --> 00:49:55,230
This is like a school trip kid getting carried away

858
00:49:56,030 --> 00:50:01,950
Did you draw this? No, I bought it

859
00:50:01,950 --> 00:50:05,910
Money talks — so the graffiti was bought?

860
00:50:05,910 --> 00:50:11,790
I was shocked at how good it is — yeah if you actually drew this it'd be impressive. Public nuisance ordinance violation.

861
00:50:11,790 --> 00:50:16,490
Yikes — I've actually reported someone to the police for this

862
00:50:16,490 --> 00:50:24,250
Please don't — I ran into someone actually drawing it

863
00:50:24,250 --> 00:50:28,590
There was someone drawing here

864
00:50:28,590 --> 00:50:31,170
That's hilarious

865
00:50:31,170 --> 00:50:33,890
They draw fast

866
00:50:33,890 --> 00:50:35,510
You can do that?

867
00:50:35,510 --> 00:50:36,950
It's like stamping stickers

868
00:50:36,950 --> 00:50:39,730
I can't tell which one is which

869
00:50:39,730 --> 00:50:41,590
I drew it for the first time just now

870
00:50:41,590 --> 00:50:44,490
Oh really?

871
00:50:44,490 --> 00:50:46,730
It'd be funny if it didn't disappear

872
00:50:46,730 --> 00:50:48,190
Yes!

873
00:50:48,190 --> 00:50:49,650
A face

874
00:50:49,650 --> 00:50:52,090
Money talks

875
00:50:52,090 --> 00:51:09,410
I didn't know how to buy it so I kept going straight from the Steam store — yeah I heard the same from another senpai, like nobody knows how to buy it — but everyone wants to spend money on it

876
00:51:09,410 --> 00:51:11,890
Yeah, this

877
00:51:11,890 --> 00:51:20,270
Everyone's wearing colorful stuff but Koyori's been in the same thing — even the sleeping bag looks plain

878
00:51:20,270 --> 00:51:26,670
It's fine. That's what makes it good.

879
00:51:26,670 --> 00:51:32,460
No no no. I don't like it.

880
00:51:32,460 --> 00:51:34,270
Oh, a white horse!

881
00:51:34,270 --> 00:51:41,950
Yeah, so since Nene said she caught it, I've been properly feeding it and taking care of it.

882
00:51:41,950 --> 00:51:45,670
But Nene hasn't come back yet.

883
00:51:45,670 --> 00:51:52,670
Four people — Nenechii, and then Nene, Anya, and Koyo... Polka, I think?

884
00:51:52,670 --> 00:51:58,340
Oh nice, looking forward to it. There wasn't anyone else who said they'd come, right?

885
00:51:58,340 --> 00:52:06,070
I don't think so. There's one person I can't see — Polka, or rather, someone invisible.

886
00:52:06,070 --> 00:52:09,070
Someone invisible? Is there a ghost?

887
00:52:09,070 --> 00:52:11,870
We're like, who's the fourth person?

888
00:52:11,870 --> 00:52:16,830
But I feel like if four of us go, it'll be over in no time.

889
00:52:16,830 --> 00:52:20,110
Like a party.

890
00:52:20,110 --> 00:52:22,530
Even three might be too many.

891
00:52:22,530 --> 00:52:25,650
I was probably going to go alone.

892
00:52:25,650 --> 00:52:32,190
I thought it was the Military Tunnel.

893
00:52:32,190 --> 00:52:34,270
When I raised my hand.

894
00:52:34,270 --> 00:52:37,890
That place is scary.

895
00:52:37,890 --> 00:52:39,250
Oh, that one's scary?

896
00:52:39,250 --> 00:52:44,580
It was intense — the enemies were really strong.

897
00:52:44,580 --> 00:52:46,580
Whoa.

898
00:52:46,580 --> 00:52:48,580
There are so many enemies there.

899
00:52:48,580 --> 00:52:51,840
Oh really, the tunnel?

900
00:52:51,840 --> 00:52:53,340
But wait, did you go there alone?

901
00:52:53,340 --> 00:52:56,520
Uh, well...

902
00:52:56,520 --> 00:53:00,920
I happened to pass by where Pekora-senpai was playing,

903
00:53:00,920 --> 00:53:02,840
and I just kind of wandered over,

904
00:53:02,840 --> 00:53:05,760
and she was like, "Wanna do a guerrilla run?"

905
00:53:05,760 --> 00:53:07,980
So I followed along and got spotted,

906
00:53:07,980 --> 00:53:13,060
and ended up being used as a meat shield,

907
00:53:13,060 --> 00:53:16,060
but she really helped me out in the end.

908
00:53:16,060 --> 00:53:18,000
Polka-senpai was super cool.

909
00:53:18,000 --> 00:53:21,280
Did I just get complimented out of nowhere?

910
00:53:21,280 --> 00:53:23,460
For real?

911
00:53:23,460 --> 00:53:26,340
Polka-senpai is so cool!

912
00:53:26,340 --> 00:53:27,530
Yay!

913
00:53:27,530 --> 00:53:30,910
I'm curious about that too, someday.

914
00:53:30,910 --> 00:53:33,670
Hm?

915
00:53:34,810 --> 00:53:37,310
I want to go back there again tonight.

916
00:53:37,310 --> 00:53:38,930
The Military Tunnel.

917
00:53:38,930 --> 00:53:41,130
Why did it get bleeped?

918
00:53:41,130 --> 00:53:42,690
The Military Tunnel is in the upper right.

919
00:53:42,690 --> 00:53:44,490
Upper right.

920
00:53:44,490 --> 00:53:47,770
Oh, this one — it says Military Tunnel.

921
00:53:47,770 --> 00:53:51,900
Where's Nene?

922
00:53:51,900 --> 00:53:54,330
It's a really long tunnel.

923
00:53:54,330 --> 00:53:56,010
Oh, it's a tunnel?

924
00:53:56,010 --> 00:54:00,610
Way deep inside.

925
00:54:00,610 --> 00:54:00,950
Red.

926
00:54:00,950 --> 00:54:02,530
The red card.

927
00:54:02,530 --> 00:54:04,530
Ah!

928
00:54:33,790 --> 00:54:54,890
So Nene got a car and drove it all the way to the house, and she said she'd set up a sleeping bag there and come back — but she never made the sleeping bag.

929
00:54:54,890 --> 00:55:00,490
Where? Wherever it is though... still.

930
00:55:00,490 --> 00:55:03,290
Is your house the same? Or not?

931
00:55:03,290 --> 00:55:08,090
It's far. It's around N, like N7 or something.

932
00:55:08,090 --> 00:55:09,890
That's far.

933
00:55:09,890 --> 00:55:11,890
It really is far.

934
00:55:11,890 --> 00:55:14,690
Near the supermarket?

935
00:55:14,690 --> 00:55:19,490
Yeah, yeah, yeah. It's convenient over there. Oh, Nene is getting closer. Nene!

936
00:55:19,490 --> 00:55:23,230
Oh right, we're a team so I can't see her.

937
00:55:23,230 --> 00:55:28,130
I see her, I see her.

938
00:55:28,130 --> 00:55:30,250
Whoa, nice!

939
00:55:30,250 --> 00:55:32,310
I could shoot if I wanted to.

940
00:55:32,310 --> 00:55:34,950
She came properly equipped.

941
00:55:34,950 --> 00:55:36,950
I could totally shoot through the sand!

942
00:55:36,950 --> 00:55:42,870
Ah, the tunnel!

943
00:55:42,870 --> 00:55:44,670
Let's gooo!

944
00:55:44,670 --> 00:55:46,470
First time making it to the last!

945
00:55:46,470 --> 00:55:48,270
Let's gooo!

946
00:55:48,270 --> 00:55:50,270
There's a bunch of colorful people having a great time.

947
00:55:50,270 --> 00:55:52,270
Everyone, I'm so happy!

948
00:55:52,270 --> 00:55:55,870
So in the end...

949
00:55:55,870 --> 00:55:56,870
I'm the senpai here, you know.

950
00:55:56,870 --> 00:55:58,670
So what about the sleeping bag?

951
00:55:58,670 --> 00:56:04,900
I made the sleeping bag and left it there.

952
00:56:05,900 --> 00:56:11,860
When this white horse comes back, it's definitely going to be gone.

953
00:56:11,860 --> 00:56:18,200
But there's nothing I can do about it now.

954
00:56:18,200 --> 00:56:21,180
What if you put a sleeping bag here too?

955
00:56:21,180 --> 00:56:24,860
Do you have any cloth?

956
00:56:24,860 --> 00:56:26,820
I don't have any cloth.

957
00:56:26,820 --> 00:56:28,560
Oh wait, let me get in the car.

958
00:56:28,560 --> 00:56:33,360
There might be cloth in the car.

959
00:56:33,360 --> 00:56:36,380
There might not be, actually.

960
00:56:36,380 --> 00:56:39,220
Hey hey, I've got something good for you!

961
00:56:39,220 --> 00:56:41,820
Here, I'll give you this.

962
00:56:41,820 --> 00:56:44,620
You just give everything away, and I just take it all.

963
00:56:44,620 --> 00:56:47,620
Finally, a horse! Oh, there's a sleeping bag!

964
00:56:47,620 --> 00:56:49,420
Whose is it?

965
00:56:49,420 --> 00:56:53,290
There's a sleeping bag here.

966
00:56:53,290 --> 00:56:54,910
Can we put it over here?

967
00:56:54,910 --> 00:57:04,830
Oh, there it is.

968
00:57:04,830 --> 00:57:07,630
Should we have him go on horseback?

969
00:57:07,630 --> 00:57:10,430
That's scary.

970
00:57:12,150 --> 00:57:14,490
Should we just let him ride the horse?

971
00:57:14,490 --> 00:57:25,880
Ania said she'd probably be a bit late or something.

972
00:57:25,880 --> 00:57:28,880
Something about going home first.

973
00:57:28,880 --> 00:57:39,040
Wait, did Koyori kill an NPC?

974
00:57:39,040 --> 00:57:40,600
She's strong!

975
00:57:40,600 --> 00:57:43,140
Oh, an NPC showed up.

976
00:57:43,140 --> 00:57:44,460
She's strong!

977
00:57:44,460 --> 00:57:46,440
Stop it!

978
00:57:46,440 --> 00:57:47,900
Don't point that at me!

979
00:57:47,900 --> 00:57:48,680
Why is it locked?

980
00:57:48,680 --> 00:57:50,800
Scary, scary, scary!

981
00:57:50,800 --> 00:57:52,690
Hm?

982
00:57:52,690 --> 00:57:54,600
Hey, Koyu-chan—

983
00:57:54,600 --> 00:57:56,400
Hm?

984
00:57:56,400 --> 00:57:58,400
You two look like a team, so when you come over here—

985
00:57:58,400 --> 00:58:00,400
I won't shoot, I won't shoot.

986
00:58:00,400 --> 00:58:02,400
Ugh, those two are a team.

987
00:58:02,400 --> 00:58:04,400
Something about the color scheme...

988
00:58:04,400 --> 00:58:06,400
She's not shooting at all.

989
00:58:06,400 --> 00:58:08,400
It's scary!

990
00:58:08,400 --> 00:58:10,200
She's really not shooting at all.

991
00:58:10,200 --> 00:58:12,200
It's scary!

992
00:58:12,200 --> 00:58:14,000
She's moving like a pro.

993
00:58:14,000 --> 00:58:18,000
Polka had never shot anyone until playing this game — people are really scary.

994
00:58:18,000 --> 00:58:20,240
I get that.

995
00:58:20,240 --> 00:58:24,520
Only in Splatoon-type games.

996
00:58:24,520 --> 00:58:26,880
Hey, keep that on me like before.

997
00:58:26,880 --> 00:58:27,720
That thing from earlier.

998
00:58:27,720 --> 00:58:29,080
Sure.

999
00:58:29,080 --> 00:58:31,920
It's Kon-Nene.

1000
00:58:31,920 --> 00:58:34,260
Um, so...

1001
00:58:34,260 --> 00:58:35,880
It's peeling, it's peeling.

1002
00:58:35,880 --> 00:58:39,920
That thing I gave you earlier—

1003
00:58:39,920 --> 00:58:41,140
The claw-like thing.

1004
00:58:41,140 --> 00:58:44,510
The hoof one.

1005
00:58:44,510 --> 00:58:44,870
Bone.

1006
00:58:44,870 --> 00:58:46,590
Bone.

1007
00:58:46,590 --> 00:58:58,140
Nice! Now it's even faster — max 65, that's 10 km/h faster than before!

1008
00:58:58,140 --> 00:59:02,720
Off it goes — so fast!

1009
00:59:02,720 --> 00:59:09,090
Oh, it's back.

1010
00:59:09,090 --> 00:59:13,880
Feels faster, right?

1011
00:59:13,880 --> 00:59:20,640
How do I get everyone on? Do I just unlock them one by one?

1012
00:59:20,640 --> 00:59:23,100
Alright, let's go!

1013
00:59:23,100 --> 00:59:29,520
Hello — oh, Annya?

1014
00:59:29,520 --> 00:59:33,360
Hello, good evening! Good evening!

1015
00:59:33,360 --> 00:59:37,900
Annya's wearing that outfit too, so it's kind of scary.

1016
00:59:37,900 --> 00:59:41,860
Nene said she was going to the bathroom and just went like that. Yeah, this outfit is super scary, isn't it?

1017
00:59:41,860 --> 00:59:47,340
Right, it's so scary. This outfit is seriously terrifying.

1018
00:59:48,350 --> 00:59:49,450
Heave-ho.

1019
00:59:49,450 --> 00:59:52,050
What should we do? Want to get on for now?

1020
00:59:52,050 --> 00:59:56,350
Ah, hold on. I need to give everyone the keys first.

1021
00:59:56,350 --> 00:59:57,850
Oh, OK!

1022
00:59:57,850 --> 00:59:58,750
Food...

1023
00:59:58,750 --> 01:00:00,970
Sure!

1024
01:00:00,970 --> 01:00:02,170
Got it.

1025
01:00:02,170 --> 01:00:07,110
Alright.

1026
01:00:07,110 --> 01:00:07,810
Oh!

1027
01:00:07,810 --> 01:00:08,910
Wait, is it burning?

1028
01:00:08,910 --> 01:00:11,210
Come here! Where are you?

1029
01:00:11,210 --> 01:00:14,160
Come here!

1030
01:00:14,160 --> 01:00:16,060
Someone's playing Graffiti.

1031
01:00:16,060 --> 01:00:20,890
Oh nice, I got to play!

1032
01:00:20,890 --> 01:00:28,990
That looks fun. Yeah, it was pretty fun.

1033
01:00:28,990 --> 01:00:35,170
Do you need to buy DLC or anything for this?

1034
01:00:35,170 --> 01:00:41,010
Yeah, you did have to buy it, but it was only like 300 yen.

1035
01:00:41,310 --> 01:00:45,750
Oh, about 300 yen. Got it, got it.

1036
01:00:45,750 --> 01:00:48,990
Six running from the driver's seat. OK, sent it.

1037
01:00:48,990 --> 01:00:52,550
Oh, welcome back. I'm heading to the bathroom like this — gave you a little scare, huh?

1038
01:00:52,550 --> 01:00:54,150
Senpai, hello!

1039
01:00:54,150 --> 01:00:58,830
There it is — oh, Anyo-chan! Where are you?

1040
01:00:58,830 --> 01:01:01,430
I'm here — behind you, behind you!

1041
01:01:01,430 --> 01:01:04,430
Behind? This one? Sorry.

1042
01:01:04,430 --> 01:01:07,670
This one, sorry.

1043
01:01:07,670 --> 01:01:09,670
That's a bit scary, come on.

1044
01:01:09,670 --> 01:01:11,470
That's a bit scary, come on.

1045
01:01:11,470 --> 01:01:13,470
I just got taken out a moment ago...

1046
01:01:13,470 --> 01:01:14,470
Oh, really?

1047
01:01:14,470 --> 01:01:16,470
Sorry, I was so close to a kill.

1048
01:01:16,470 --> 01:01:19,270
Yeah, I was so close to a kill.

1049
01:01:19,270 --> 01:01:22,270
I went through the air road without thinking.

1050
01:01:22,270 --> 01:01:24,070
Sorry to keep you waiting!

1051
01:01:24,070 --> 01:01:26,990
Where did you go? What happened?

1052
01:01:26,990 --> 01:01:31,670
I was trying to hunt a boar to make a sleeping bag...

1053
01:01:31,670 --> 01:01:32,670
Good thinking!

1054
01:01:32,670 --> 01:01:34,670
There were none around. Sorry, I was wandering about.

1055
01:01:34,670 --> 01:01:36,670
They're never there when you look, huh?

1056
01:01:36,670 --> 01:01:38,670
I got it ready for you to ride.

1057
01:01:38,670 --> 01:01:40,470
Senpai Renes!

1058
01:01:40,470 --> 01:01:42,270
Here, take this.

1059
01:01:42,270 --> 01:01:44,270
As an apology.

1060
01:01:44,270 --> 01:01:46,070
Here, take this.

1061
01:01:46,070 --> 01:01:47,870
An apology?

1062
01:01:47,870 --> 01:01:49,870
Temptation chocolate!

1063
01:01:49,870 --> 01:01:51,670
Thank you!

1064
01:01:51,670 --> 01:01:53,670
A cake!

1065
01:01:53,670 --> 01:01:55,470
Can everyone get on?

1066
01:01:55,470 --> 01:01:57,270
Can't get on.

1067
01:01:57,270 --> 01:01:59,270
Can't get on?

1068
01:01:59,270 --> 01:02:01,270
It's not unlocked.

1069
01:02:01,270 --> 01:02:03,270
It's unlocked now.

1070
01:02:03,270 --> 01:02:05,270
The back isn't open?

1071
01:02:05,270 --> 01:02:07,270
I'm on!

1072
01:02:07,270 --> 01:02:09,150
Oh, so that's how you get on.

1073
01:02:09,150 --> 01:02:11,070
I'm on, I'm on!

1074
01:02:11,070 --> 01:02:13,870
I've never had this many people on at once.

1075
01:02:13,870 --> 01:02:15,870
Let's go!

1076
01:02:15,870 --> 01:02:17,670
Yeah!

1077
01:02:17,670 --> 01:02:19,470
It's Cap, it's Cap!

1078
01:02:19,470 --> 01:02:21,470
Let's go!

1079
01:02:21,470 --> 01:02:23,470
Party party party night!

1080
01:02:23,470 --> 01:02:25,470
The windshield is cracked, though.

1081
01:02:25,470 --> 01:02:27,270
Well, that happens sometimes.

1082
01:02:27,270 --> 01:02:29,070
Did Koyo do that?

1083
01:02:29,070 --> 01:02:31,730
Give Koyori more credit!

1084
01:02:31,730 --> 01:02:34,070
That body over there — that was Koyori's work.

1085
01:02:34,070 --> 01:02:36,430
Yeah, that body is Koyori's.

1086
01:02:36,430 --> 01:02:37,910
No, I got phased through again.

1087
01:02:37,910 --> 01:02:42,620
You phased through? I only had an incendiary and a flare.

1088
01:02:42,620 --> 01:02:44,110
Are you serious?

1089
01:02:44,110 --> 01:02:46,510
Oh, is that Carl and Ichios?

1090
01:02:46,510 --> 01:02:49,130
Yeah, that's them — they're down below right now!

1091
01:02:49,130 --> 01:02:50,230
A bear!

1092
01:02:50,230 --> 01:02:52,630
Look, a bear!

1093
01:02:52,630 --> 01:02:54,810
This is probably... I wanna fight the bear!

1094
01:02:54,810 --> 01:02:55,510
Come here!

1095
01:02:55,510 --> 01:02:56,990
No good!

1096
01:02:56,990 --> 01:02:58,030
Huh? A bear? What?

1097
01:02:58,030 --> 01:02:59,510
Oh, is a drink coming in?

1098
01:02:59,510 --> 01:03:01,190
Oh no, oh no!

1099
01:03:01,190 --> 01:03:02,720
We can't take on the bear!

1100
01:03:02,720 --> 01:03:03,610
We made it!

1101
01:03:03,610 --> 01:03:06,290
This is not a 'we made it' situation!

1102
01:03:06,290 --> 01:03:07,910
Everyone get off!

1103
01:03:07,910 --> 01:03:09,920
Yes sir!

1104
01:03:09,920 --> 01:03:11,330
I wanna fight the bear, the bear!

1105
01:03:11,330 --> 01:03:13,950
Oh, did you stop by? Nice!

1106
01:03:13,950 --> 01:03:16,570
Maybe they stopped by Anikurason?

1107
01:03:16,570 --> 01:03:18,070
Wait, wait, wait!

1108
01:03:18,070 --> 01:03:19,570
What are you holding while lying down?

1109
01:03:19,570 --> 01:03:20,750
Wait, why, why, why?

1110
01:03:20,750 --> 01:03:22,010
Why are you holding a paddle?

1111
01:03:22,010 --> 01:03:22,870
Lie down, Chi!

1112
01:03:22,870 --> 01:03:24,630
Just do that thing.

1113
01:03:24,630 --> 01:03:27,970
Please don't dig up Koyori.

1114
01:03:27,970 --> 01:03:29,770
Go, go!

1115
01:03:29,770 --> 01:03:31,370
Oh, it came off!

1116
01:03:31,370 --> 01:03:32,310
It comes off.

1117
01:03:32,310 --> 01:03:35,130
That's for real — you going with that?

1118
01:03:35,130 --> 01:03:37,570
Alright, let's go everyone!

1119
01:03:37,570 --> 01:03:39,270
Going with these two.

1120
01:03:39,270 --> 01:03:40,770
Alright then.

1121
01:03:40,770 --> 01:03:42,970
Hey hey, Chimin, sleeping bag

1122
01:03:42,970 --> 01:03:44,670
Huh? Can't do the sleeping bag

1123
01:03:44,670 --> 01:03:46,210
You're giving me a sleeping bag?

1124
01:03:46,210 --> 01:03:48,170
Yeah, might be better to leave the sleeping bag there

1125
01:03:48,170 --> 01:03:50,970
If you're holding a sleeping bag while filming, they'll come dig up your body

1126
01:03:50,970 --> 01:03:54,970
They're gonna come dig up your body?!

1127
01:03:54,970 --> 01:03:57,770
That's terrifying

1128
01:03:57,770 --> 01:04:01,770
That means you can fight, Nene-senpai

1129
01:04:01,770 --> 01:04:04,770
You can fight with this, right

1130
01:04:04,770 --> 01:04:09,480
Everyone went to go place their bags at their spots

1131
01:04:09,480 --> 01:04:13,360
It wouldn't work unless it was pretty far away

1132
01:04:13,360 --> 01:04:15,300
Nah

1133
01:04:15,300 --> 01:04:21,370
Oh, nah

1134
01:04:21,370 --> 01:04:23,370
Can't go

1135
01:04:23,370 --> 01:04:29,500
Are you starting already, Koyori?

1136
01:04:29,500 --> 01:04:31,420
It's already started!

1137
01:04:31,420 --> 01:04:34,420
Why are you starting a party by yourself?

1138
01:04:34,420 --> 01:04:38,820
I saw someone so I shot

1139
01:04:38,820 --> 01:04:40,820
Don't start a party on your own!

1140
01:04:40,820 --> 01:04:44,620
I partied!

1141
01:04:44,620 --> 01:04:46,620
You started the party way too early

1142
01:04:48,420 --> 01:04:50,580
Oh wait, it wasn't them

1143
01:04:50,580 --> 01:04:52,440
Bang bang bang bang bang

1144
01:04:52,440 --> 01:05:02,930
Everyone scattered on the spot

1145
01:05:02,930 --> 01:05:08,010
We ended up splitting up on the spot

1146
01:05:08,010 --> 01:05:23,740
Everything's too close together, can't place it

1147
01:05:23,740 --> 01:05:25,180
Seriously?

1148
01:05:25,180 --> 01:05:28,620
Can't we split it at Polka's place?

1149
01:05:28,620 --> 01:05:31,400
So you can't transfer ownership to Polka after all?

1150
01:05:31,900 --> 01:05:37,890
Oh, if the friend thing doesn't pop up, you can't drop the ward?

1151
01:05:37,890 --> 01:05:41,230
Oh, I pushed it

1152
01:05:41,230 --> 01:05:44,170
Oh, but—

1153
01:05:44,170 --> 01:05:47,350
Should we just charge in while we're still on it?

1154
01:05:47,350 --> 01:05:49,110
Oh, welcome back

1155
01:05:49,110 --> 01:05:51,690
Okay

1156
01:05:51,690 --> 01:05:56,150
What's that guy doing

1157
01:05:56,150 --> 01:05:58,710
Oh, you're going with that?

1158
01:05:58,710 --> 01:06:00,130
Go ahead

1159
01:06:00,130 --> 01:06:01,930
Isn't this a Paddle?

1160
01:06:01,930 --> 01:06:06,730
That one's a Paddle

1161
01:06:06,730 --> 01:06:10,530
What was this again? This gun

1162
01:06:10,530 --> 01:06:12,330
Machine gun

1163
01:06:12,330 --> 01:06:13,330
Machine gun?

1164
01:06:13,330 --> 01:06:14,330
The one I opened earlier was totally different

1165
01:06:14,330 --> 01:06:18,130
Is it an LMG or something? Was it an LMG?

1166
01:06:18,130 --> 01:06:20,930
The name? This one

1167
01:06:20,930 --> 01:06:24,530
HMLMG

1168
01:06:24,530 --> 01:06:26,530
Right right, HM-something

1169
01:06:26,530 --> 01:06:30,330
Huh, it's got something interesting on it

1170
01:06:30,330 --> 01:06:31,930
Alright, let's go

1171
01:06:31,930 --> 01:06:33,930
I feel like the minigun can fire a ton of shots

1172
01:06:33,930 --> 01:06:35,930
Like, what? Huh?

1173
01:06:35,930 --> 01:06:37,930
Took one down

1174
01:06:37,930 --> 01:06:39,730
Scary

1175
01:06:39,730 --> 01:06:41,730
Who's already fighting?

1176
01:06:41,730 --> 01:06:43,730
Already took one down

1177
01:06:43,730 --> 01:06:45,730
Gotta take them down at this range

1178
01:06:45,730 --> 01:06:47,530
Done

1179
01:06:47,530 --> 01:06:51,330
It's turning into a competition for who can take down the most today

1180
01:06:53,130 --> 01:06:55,110
Moving in!

1181
01:06:55,110 --> 01:07:01,880
Woohoo!

1182
01:07:01,880 --> 01:07:09,280
Okay, I've got a feel for it

1183
01:07:09,280 --> 01:07:10,280
They're getting close, they're getting close!

1184
01:07:10,280 --> 01:07:12,280
Huh? They disappeared

1185
01:07:12,280 --> 01:07:14,280
It's hitting right in front

1186
01:07:14,280 --> 01:07:21,070
Oh, no hesitation at all

1187
01:07:21,070 --> 01:07:25,470
Hey, Paddle, get moving!

1188
01:07:26,270 --> 01:07:28,270
Paddle!

1189
01:07:28,270 --> 01:07:31,510
The Paddle user isn't going first?!

1190
01:07:31,510 --> 01:07:33,330
I only have 16 HP!

1191
01:07:33,330 --> 01:07:41,950
This time Nene is

1192
01:07:41,950 --> 01:07:44,750
going to be the key

1193
01:07:44,750 --> 01:07:50,890
They're really hiding just their head

1194
01:07:50,890 --> 01:07:56,820
It bounces around a lot, doesn't it

1195
01:07:56,820 --> 01:08:01,930
Is this side better?

1196
01:08:01,930 --> 01:08:03,930
Feels like you'd get hit with the puzzle

1197
01:08:03,930 --> 01:08:51,540
Ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow ow!

1198
01:08:51,540 --> 01:08:57,850
It's getting dark

1199
01:08:57,850 --> 01:09:04,890
Yeah, you're right

1200
01:09:04,890 --> 01:09:11,430
You're right there!

1201
01:09:11,430 --> 01:09:14,340
That was close!

1202
01:09:14,340 --> 01:09:22,630
But the people—

1203
01:09:22,630 --> 01:09:25,230
Where's the goal?

1204
01:09:25,230 --> 01:09:31,000
Are there still more?

1205
01:09:31,000 --> 01:09:35,000
Still some left. One person was hiding in the middle.

1206
01:09:35,000 --> 01:09:38,000
I don't know where they are now.

1207
01:09:38,000 --> 01:09:41,800
I don't think there were 10 people to begin with.

1208
01:09:41,800 --> 01:09:43,800
Toward the back.

1209
01:09:43,800 --> 01:09:46,600
Yeah, I don't think there were 10.

1210
01:09:46,600 --> 01:09:51,780
This area's probably an easy one.

1211
01:09:51,780 --> 01:09:54,900
Oh, so there's difficulty levels.

1212
01:09:54,900 --> 01:09:57,700
Let's go!

1213
01:09:57,700 --> 01:10:02,500
Whoa, everyone's getting knocked down!

1214
01:10:02,500 --> 01:10:04,600
Oh!

1215
01:10:04,600 --> 01:10:25,690
Koyori's lane!

1216
01:10:25,690 --> 01:10:28,330
I ended up standing in Koyori's lane!

1217
01:10:28,330 --> 01:10:30,600
Sorry!

1218
01:10:30,600 --> 01:10:32,880
There's still one more, probably.

1219
01:10:32,880 --> 01:10:39,520
Where? Where?

1220
01:10:39,520 --> 01:10:41,280
I think I got them!

1221
01:10:41,280 --> 01:10:42,500
Where are they?

1222
01:10:42,500 --> 01:10:43,580
Oh, are there still more?

1223
01:10:43,580 --> 01:10:44,980
Sorry!

1224
01:10:44,980 --> 01:10:46,780
Nice! Nice job, everyone!

1225
01:10:46,780 --> 01:10:49,820
Sounds like someone's saying something.

1226
01:10:49,820 --> 01:10:57,150
I'm doing stuff but none of it is hitting!

1227
01:10:57,150 --> 01:11:01,550
Oh, got one! Got one!

1228
01:11:01,550 --> 01:11:03,550
I'm gonna die! I'm gonna die!

1229
01:11:03,550 --> 01:11:11,670
Is that everyone?

1230
01:11:11,670 --> 01:11:13,570
Nice!

1231
01:11:13,570 --> 01:11:15,470
Nicely done!

1232
01:11:15,470 --> 01:11:17,470
We're done! We're done!

1233
01:11:17,470 --> 01:11:21,610
We finished!

1234
01:11:21,610 --> 01:11:24,650
We're done though.

1235
01:11:24,650 --> 01:11:27,950
It's so dark I can't tell what's going on.

1236
01:11:27,950 --> 01:11:33,120
I can't even tell where anything is.

1237
01:11:33,120 --> 01:11:43,150
It's so dark.

1238
01:11:43,150 --> 01:11:47,970
Where do you fire missiles from?

1239
01:11:47,970 --> 01:11:51,870
Here, this. But the missiles — the ammo, you know.

1240
01:11:51,870 --> 01:11:56,550
How many do you have? I barely have any at all.

1241
01:11:56,550 --> 01:11:58,710
I have zero missiles right now.

1242
01:11:58,710 --> 01:12:01,570
You have to collect them, right? That's impressive.

1243
01:12:01,570 --> 01:12:03,410
Like Peko-chan — she's amazing.

1244
01:12:03,410 --> 01:12:06,910
They only drop from elite boxes, apparently.

1245
01:12:06,910 --> 01:12:07,950
Oh really?

1246
01:12:07,950 --> 01:12:09,950
I can't get to those strong areas.

1247
01:12:09,950 --> 01:12:10,330
Ah.

1248
01:12:10,330 --> 01:12:11,210
Yeah.

1249
01:12:11,210 --> 01:12:12,550
Oh, still riding.

1250
01:12:12,550 --> 01:12:14,230
What's over there?

1251
01:12:14,230 --> 01:12:27,730
Apparently you can use this to precisely bomb spots in the city.

1252
01:12:27,730 --> 01:12:31,530
Wow, that's amazing!

1253
01:12:31,530 --> 01:12:34,930
I want missiles.

1254
01:12:34,930 --> 01:12:41,390
I totally get the desire to collect missiles.

1255
01:12:41,390 --> 01:12:44,910
But from far away, right?

1256
01:12:44,910 --> 01:12:46,410
It's tough.

1257
01:12:46,410 --> 01:12:51,170
If you can handle the NPCs, you can do it from far away.

1258
01:12:51,170 --> 01:12:52,090
True.

1259
01:12:52,090 --> 01:12:55,090
Whoa, that's scary!

1260
01:12:55,090 --> 01:12:57,030
And it's dark.

1261
01:12:57,030 --> 01:12:59,690
Apparently she had missiles earlier.

1262
01:12:59,690 --> 01:13:04,300
Huh? Missiles?

1263
01:13:04,300 --> 01:13:07,340
Why do you say "apparently she had them"?

1264
01:13:07,340 --> 01:13:17,510
Are they gone already?

1265
01:13:17,510 --> 01:13:20,910
What's an elite box, anyway?

1266
01:13:20,910 --> 01:13:24,020
A missile dropped in 15 minutes? That's crazy!

1267
01:13:24,020 --> 01:13:27,340
Probability-wise — oh, I have to stay on this.

1268
01:13:27,340 --> 01:13:29,910
I haven't been winning at all.

1269
01:13:29,910 --> 01:13:31,410
Hey everyone, like—

1270
01:13:31,410 --> 01:13:33,260
I'm not on yet.

1271
01:13:33,260 --> 01:13:36,910
Oh, but like — Busshi, Asa, Asa, Asarina?

1272
01:13:36,910 --> 01:13:38,410
Busshi and Asarina?

1273
01:13:38,410 --> 01:13:40,210
They're all swarming around.

1274
01:13:40,210 --> 01:13:43,090
Are they lighting the way?

1275
01:13:43,510 --> 01:14:13,890
Oh, I turned into a clam! Oh, sorry! Sorry! Sorry! Huh? Huh? Did you run me over? Did I disappear? No, I just pulled my foot back. I'm alive, I'm alive, it's fine. Looks like you were scared. That hurt so much! Oh, I'm sorry! You actually look super comfortable in there.

1276
01:14:13,890 --> 01:14:20,200
There's nothing good here.

1277
01:14:20,200 --> 01:14:26,340
Yeah, nothing good.

1278
01:14:26,340 --> 01:14:30,400
There's really not much here.

1279
01:14:30,400 --> 01:14:34,540
Yeah, I figured. Well, makes sense.

1280
01:14:34,540 --> 01:14:40,510
We're so close to the center, after all.

1281
01:14:40,510 --> 01:14:44,720
That easily

1282
01:14:47,440 --> 01:14:53,030
I wonder if they'll come

1283
01:14:53,030 --> 01:15:02,910
Oh right, this is a missile launch site to begin with

1284
01:15:02,910 --> 01:15:10,690
So it's not great?

1285
01:15:10,690 --> 01:15:24,510
It feels like it's working a little

1286
01:15:24,510 --> 01:15:34,250
Oh, this is interesting

1287
01:15:34,250 --> 01:15:40,880
There's nothing here, for real

1288
01:15:40,880 --> 01:15:47,610
There ain't nothin' here

1289
01:15:47,870 --> 01:15:54,530
Right?

1290
01:15:54,530 --> 01:16:07,510
All we got was the sense of accomplishment and the experience of actually doing something

1291
01:16:07,510 --> 01:16:12,230
Hey hey, we're a team, okay? Hey hey!

1292
01:16:12,230 --> 01:16:15,090
Cheering each other on is important

1293
01:16:15,090 --> 01:16:20,030
Let's do our best going forward

1294
01:16:20,030 --> 01:16:24,480
Even if we only have 8 bullets left

1295
01:16:24,480 --> 01:16:27,570
Hey hey

1296
01:16:28,150 --> 01:16:34,310
Hey? What? Ow ow ow!

1297
01:16:34,310 --> 01:16:40,180
The helicopter is here after all! Disarm!

1298
01:16:40,180 --> 01:16:57,270
Here we go! Is everyone doing okay?

1299
01:16:57,270 --> 01:17:00,400
Come to think of it

1300
01:17:00,400 --> 01:17:07,740
Busou Renkin

1301
01:17:08,060 --> 01:17:10,580
Oh, a holographic sight.

1302
01:17:10,580 --> 01:17:20,250
The official hololive one.

1303
01:17:20,250 --> 01:17:23,180
Is everyone safe?

1304
01:17:23,180 --> 01:17:28,500
Everyone safe?

1305
01:17:28,500 --> 01:17:35,780
Safe?

1306
01:17:35,780 --> 01:17:42,520
This is Polka's car, it was here. Thank goodness. Polka was left behind.

1307
01:17:42,520 --> 01:17:46,040
You doing okay? You alright? Has everyone gone home already?

1308
01:17:46,040 --> 01:17:48,920
Did the good ones already leave?

1309
01:17:48,920 --> 01:17:53,210
Did they go home already?

1310
01:17:53,210 --> 01:17:59,610
Did they leave?

1311
01:17:59,610 --> 01:18:02,210
E-everyone!

1312
01:18:02,210 --> 01:18:10,530
Did we all just scatter?

1313
01:18:10,530 --> 01:18:27,140
Everyone, did you go home?

1314
01:18:27,140 --> 01:18:31,060
I was running from the helicopter

1315
01:18:31,060 --> 01:18:34,200
Did they go home?

1316
01:18:34,200 --> 01:18:41,600
Hey, if Koyori is here today, who is Koyori teamed up with?

1317
01:18:41,600 --> 01:18:43,600
Wait, did Nene just die?

1318
01:18:43,600 --> 01:18:48,950
I got taken out!

1319
01:18:48,950 --> 01:18:58,950
It's okay. It's okay.

1320
01:18:58,950 --> 01:19:01,800
Dismissed!

1321
01:19:10,140 --> 01:19:12,140
Is Koyo alone?

1322
01:19:12,140 --> 01:19:16,940
I was thinking I wanted to raid Koyori

1323
01:19:16,940 --> 01:19:29,360
I don't know

1324
01:19:29,360 --> 01:19:31,020
Like, kind of

1325
01:19:31,020 --> 01:19:34,020
I don't know how many supplies Koyori has

1326
01:19:34,020 --> 01:19:37,010
I wonder how long Koyori can fight alone

1327
01:19:37,010 --> 01:19:38,820
As for Polka

1328
01:19:38,820 --> 01:19:45,890
Fully geared?

1329
01:19:45,890 --> 01:19:47,890
Well if she's fully geared

1330
01:19:47,890 --> 01:19:49,690
I think

1331
01:19:49,690 --> 01:19:52,490
She'd probably be happier being attacked

1332
01:19:52,490 --> 01:19:57,810
I dunno

1333
01:19:57,810 --> 01:20:03,860
Good work everyone, what good kids they all are

1334
01:20:03,860 --> 01:20:10,460
She's good at sniping

1335
01:20:10,460 --> 01:20:16,240
Our remaining firepower is just Nene

1336
01:20:16,240 --> 01:20:21,220
Give Nene something to use

1337
01:20:21,760 --> 01:20:24,220
What should we do

1338
01:20:24,220 --> 01:20:33,270
This is a tough call

1339
01:20:33,270 --> 01:20:37,390
I wonder what Haley is doing

1340
01:20:37,390 --> 01:20:40,970
Haley just came to hang out

1341
01:20:40,970 --> 01:20:43,370
Wait, hold on

1342
01:20:43,370 --> 01:20:45,690
Is she chasing Nene? Is she okay?

1343
01:20:45,690 --> 01:20:49,730
I was surprised, I thought she was chasing Nene

1344
01:20:49,730 --> 01:20:58,340
Nene, just get in the car

1345
01:20:58,480 --> 01:21:00,480
There's a paddle!

1346
01:21:00,480 --> 01:21:03,280
Nene, get in!

1347
01:21:03,280 --> 01:21:13,210
She's always out there doing GTA stuff on her own

1348
01:21:13,210 --> 01:21:18,010
Hmm, I feel like we might lose

1349
01:21:18,010 --> 01:21:21,810
How much do we have — oh, we have nothing

1350
01:21:21,810 --> 01:21:26,610
Metal Fragments, no wait, what was it — Fragments

1351
01:21:27,410 --> 01:21:32,400
How much of what should I bring

1352
01:21:32,400 --> 01:21:42,040
The fact that I'm even asking means Polka is probably the weakest link

1353
01:21:42,040 --> 01:21:48,460
Can't break through the wall. I see.

1354
01:21:48,460 --> 01:21:52,410
Rocket launcher

1355
01:21:52,410 --> 01:21:59,440
After checking out Koyori's base

1356
01:21:59,440 --> 01:22:06,570
I managed to make a C4, but not a gun

1357
01:22:07,150 --> 01:22:09,150
Oh, a base for raiding?

