1638
01:45:19,320 --> 01:45:27,010
Oh wait, never mind, I was surprised. It's not Polka.

1639
01:45:27,010 --> 01:45:34,210
She one-shotted someone? Well, even if it's not Polka, what are we even talking about? I'm so curious.

1640
01:45:34,210 --> 01:45:40,610
Like, those random bits of chat popping up here and there — the content is so intriguing.

1641
01:45:40,610 --> 01:45:43,610
Yikes

1642
01:45:43,610 --> 01:45:48,350
How many years have I been looking for this horse

1643
01:45:48,350 --> 01:45:52,410
So she didn't reply to Polka. Then I'll go first—

1644
01:45:52,410 --> 01:45:55,140
She prioritized me over Polka. Oh—

1645
01:45:55,140 --> 01:46:01,470
This is Nene's car's storage

1646
01:46:01,470 --> 01:46:08,510
If I buy Nene a car with storage, the Nimo-pan situation would be solved

1647
01:46:08,510 --> 01:46:12,780
Riding my beloved car again after a while feels kinda...

1648
01:46:12,780 --> 01:46:19,160
nice. I hadn't been riding it lately, just doing maintenance runs.

1649
01:46:19,160 --> 01:46:28,940
Riding it again after so long, I was like, wow horses are cute. Isn't it that way? More like around this high-radiation area where something

1650
01:46:28,940 --> 01:46:32,360
Where was it... I feel like something's around here

1651
01:46:32,360 --> 01:46:37,690
Oh, the pumpkin-growing festival zone

1652
