1880
02:04:44,650 --> 02:04:45,530
The parts.

1881
02:04:45,530 --> 02:04:47,510
It's the best.

1882
02:04:47,510 --> 02:04:49,760
I want this one next.

1883
02:04:49,760 --> 02:04:52,010
I'm slowly starting to feel like a dealer.

1884
02:04:52,010 --> 02:04:54,070
Wonder if I could sell cars.

1885
02:04:54,070 --> 02:04:55,410
As a job.

1886
02:04:55,410 --> 02:05:01,420
Yeah, quite.

1887
02:05:01,420 --> 02:05:03,440
There are all kinds of different parts,

1888
02:05:03,440 --> 02:05:05,100
and you can go up to like 4 modules,

1889
02:05:05,100 --> 02:05:06,080
and build it.

1890
02:05:06,080 --> 02:05:07,280
And then

1891
02:05:07,280 --> 02:05:10,160
2 modules—

1892
02:05:10,160 --> 02:05:12,760
attach 2 storage units

1893
02:05:12,760 --> 02:05:13,640
to a car.

1894
02:05:13,640 --> 02:05:21,240
So you can fit double the normal inventory space in this one.

1895
02:05:21,240 --> 02:05:29,860
There are cars that can hold two of them.

1896
02:05:29,860 --> 02:05:36,530
Oh, whose place is that?

1897
02:05:36,530 --> 02:05:39,330
Is this Koyori's place?

1898
02:05:39,330 --> 02:05:44,720
Wait, it's near a cave — isn't this Koyori's house?

1899
02:05:44,720 --> 02:05:49,810
Maybe not.

1900
02:05:49,810 --> 02:05:58,750
No, if it were Koyuri's house it'd be a bit more… whose house is this?

1901
02:05:58,750 --> 02:06:01,750
A trash can!

1902
02:06:01,750 --> 02:06:05,690
That's a fancy trash can.

1903
02:06:05,690 --> 02:06:09,770
Isn't Koyuri's house over that way, probably?

1904
02:06:09,770 --> 02:06:12,650
So many mushrooms!

1905
02:06:12,650 --> 02:06:17,520
Koyuri's house is over there, probably.

1906
02:06:17,520 --> 02:06:19,320
I should remember that.

1907
02:06:19,320 --> 02:06:20,880
There's so much to remember.

1908
02:06:20,880 --> 02:06:22,720
Impossible.

1909
02:06:22,720 --> 02:06:36,710
Parking the car near the house brings back bad memories, so that's no good.

1910
02:06:36,710 --> 02:06:45,320
Nene's horse.

1911
02:06:45,320 --> 02:06:46,580
No food.

1912
02:06:46,580 --> 02:06:48,400
Not my problem.

1913
02:06:48,400 --> 02:06:53,690
Good luck.

1914
02:06:53,690 --> 02:07:01,640
You're the one who said you wanted to keep it.

1915
02:07:01,640 --> 02:07:04,160
Feed it and walk it yourself.

1916
02:07:14,270 --> 02:07:15,590
I made a mistake.

1917
02:07:15,590 --> 02:07:17,190
Huh? What? What did you get wrong?

1918
02:07:17,190 --> 02:07:20,990
Oh, I didn't switch to team chat.

1919
02:07:20,990 --> 02:07:24,350
That's embarrassing.

1920
02:07:24,350 --> 02:07:25,990
Bzzt bzzt bzzt bzzt.

1921
02:07:25,990 --> 02:07:35,660
So

1922
02:07:35,660 --> 02:07:39,980
Would they buy a horse that has no food? I mean, that's true—

1923
02:07:39,980 --> 02:07:43,180
saying it has no food, that it won't eat—

1924
02:07:43,180 --> 02:07:45,120
means there's no food for it

1925
02:07:45,520 --> 02:07:48,820
Can they really buy a horse with no food?

1926
02:07:48,820 --> 02:07:51,840
Could it be...

1927
02:07:51,840 --> 02:07:53,620
if we follow that logic

1928
02:07:53,620 --> 02:08:04,360
Respawn the horse!

1929
02:08:04,360 --> 02:08:14,010
If there's no

1930
02:08:14,010 --> 02:08:16,930
food, I'll buy it

1931
02:08:16,930 --> 02:08:18,970
How much?

1932
02:08:18,970 --> 02:08:26,170
Well, it has no food after all

1933
02:08:26,170 --> 02:08:41,690
Alright everyone, drink some water

1934
02:08:44,440 --> 02:08:50,380
That guy's messing around

1935
02:08:50,380 --> 02:08:53,640
That guy's something else

1936
02:08:53,640 --> 02:09:01,980
That guy's probably still in elementary school

1937
02:09:01,980 --> 02:09:11,260
More than that, it'd probably be faster to just go to Nene's place and throw money at her and say "I'll buy it with this"

1938
02:09:11,260 --> 02:09:15,830
Like, "here, take this"

1939
02:09:16,230 --> 02:09:22,990
This is the military tone... oh, they dropped the price by 1000 yen

1940
02:09:22,990 --> 02:09:34,280
The name would change though, probably

1941
02:09:34,280 --> 02:09:38,080
Oh wow, this is something

1942
02:09:38,080 --> 02:09:40,440
Who's that

1943
02:09:40,440 --> 02:09:45,770
Is that white-haired Nikomachi?

1944
02:09:46,070 --> 02:09:52,540
If we wait a bit more, will the price drop? Nene, Nene

1945
02:09:52,540 --> 02:09:59,380
If we leave it alone a bit longer, will it drop the price on its own?

1946
02:09:59,380 --> 02:10:08,290
The name being different is a bit of a problem though

1947
02:10:08,290 --> 02:10:18,780
Nene fell asleep. She got sleepy. Aww, sleepy Nene

1948
02:10:18,780 --> 02:10:28,880
So that means we can get it for free, right?

1949
02:10:29,680 --> 02:10:39,400
Well, when you go looking, you can never find one

1950
02:10:39,400 --> 02:10:50,130
The same horse probably doesn't respawn in the same spot

1951
02:10:50,130 --> 02:11:01,380
We've come pretty far from base. It'd be a pain to bring it back even if we found one around here

1952
02:11:01,380 --> 02:11:15,950
Matsui-san must live in quite a remote area

1953
02:11:15,950 --> 02:11:21,930
Well, Nene— oh, Nene fell asleep. This is starting to feel like Monster Hunter

1954
02:11:21,930 --> 02:11:30,290
Confirmed Nene's offline, said "Nene's asleep," and now the horse is in a capturable state. This is it.

1955
02:11:30,290 --> 02:11:33,800
The horse.

1956
02:11:33,800 --> 02:11:43,960
Whoa, it came this way. Near the fishing spot?

1957
02:11:43,960 --> 02:11:49,090
That's a deer.

1958
02:11:49,090 --> 02:11:55,910
Alright, trap. Get the trap ready. Who's got a trap? I'm throwing the tranquilizer—

1959
02:11:55,910 --> 02:11:58,710
Looks like it could work

1960
02:11:58,710 --> 02:12:06,250
Well, this is a good lesson for Nene about the impermanence of commerce

1961
02:12:06,250 --> 02:12:12,150
And we gave her steel too, so this is a win. We won this one.

1962
02:12:12,150 --> 02:12:16,410
Polka wins

1963
02:12:16,410 --> 02:12:22,790
We won this

1964
02:12:22,790 --> 02:12:27,030
We've come this far

1965
02:12:27,550 --> 02:12:40,330
Whoa, please watch the screen. Press it. Hit the warning. Press it.

1966
02:12:40,330 --> 02:12:47,490
Whoa, watch out for rollovers~

1967
02:12:47,490 --> 02:12:52,340
Gotta call them.

1968
02:12:52,340 --> 02:12:57,100
Gotta make a call.

1969
02:13:04,040 --> 02:13:10,600
Lunaitan? Lunaitan has one? I wonder what kind of horse Lunaitan has

1970
02:13:10,600 --> 02:13:13,180
Whoa— what's that?

1971
02:13:13,180 --> 02:13:19,280
Lunaitan, it's like a repeating everyday thing

1972
02:13:19,280 --> 02:13:27,610
If Lunaitan has a horse, then well, you know

1973
02:13:27,610 --> 02:13:33,470
Depending on the color, we could trade with Nene's

1974
02:13:33,830 --> 02:13:45,310
Hey, what is this home base

1975
02:13:45,310 --> 02:13:50,210
Oh, it's raining, isn't it

1976
02:13:50,210 --> 02:13:52,930
Oh—

1977
02:13:52,930 --> 02:13:56,410
Hmm... ohhhh

1978
02:13:56,410 --> 02:14:00,110
Rain, rain

1979
02:14:00,110 --> 02:14:06,390
Whoa, this site is amazing, like really amazing

1980
02:14:06,710 --> 02:14:14,870
This isn't me! This isn't Polka!

1981
02:14:14,870 --> 02:14:19,340
This is not Polka! This isn't me! Not this time!

1982
02:14:19,340 --> 02:14:23,510
Oh no! This is going to get clipped! Malicious out-of-context clips incoming!

1983
02:14:23,510 --> 02:14:30,260
Polka! Two horses! Oh no oh no oh no! Run run run!

1984
02:14:30,260 --> 02:14:40,850
If you do it right you can pull it off!

1985
02:14:41,010 --> 02:14:49,080
Are these the EN members? So, does everyone have a horse?

1986
02:14:49,080 --> 02:14:52,320
What do you think?

1987
02:14:52,320 --> 02:14:58,020
Hello. Oh, does it look similar?

1988
02:14:58,020 --> 02:15:01,980
It's Pinto-kun!

1989
02:15:01,980 --> 02:15:08,620
Well, it's not quite Pinto-kun.

1990
02:15:09,100 --> 02:15:15,820
Ito-kun was a bit similar but the name's different too. If both the name and color are random, we're done for

1991
02:15:15,820 --> 02:15:19,420
At some point I really need to just compromise

1992
02:15:19,420 --> 02:15:25,050
Wait, is this Subaru's house? It's become such a nice place

1993
02:15:25,050 --> 02:15:30,260
Looks like it has good ventilation

1994
02:15:30,260 --> 02:15:38,520
Feels like you could throw something in there

1995
02:15:38,520 --> 02:15:41,720
Was this place abandoned?

1996
02:15:41,920 --> 02:16:01,300
Then maybe we should throw something in.

1997
02:16:01,300 --> 02:16:05,560
But if this place was abandoned, then what about the horse?

1998
02:16:05,560 --> 02:16:12,980
Wait, why is there a horse?

1999
02:16:12,980 --> 02:16:14,060
Doesn't that seem weird?

2000
02:16:14,060 --> 02:16:29,900
Why, why is there a horse?

2001
02:16:29,900 --> 02:16:33,070
And on top of that,

2002
02:16:33,070 --> 02:16:36,170
this house is way too rough,

2003
02:16:36,170 --> 02:16:40,090
way too rough.

2004
02:16:40,090 --> 02:16:46,940
This one's tricky.

2005
02:16:46,940 --> 02:16:50,780
This is just too...

2006
02:16:50,780 --> 02:17:03,550
If you do it this way, you can't get out — the driveway's blocked.

2007
02:17:03,550 --> 02:17:16,480
Ah, it didn't go in.

2008
02:17:16,480 --> 02:17:21,040
You're taking damage! Ugh, can't get it in right.

2009
02:17:21,040 --> 02:17:23,670
Just like a horse — can't get in either.

2010
02:17:23,670 --> 02:17:28,620
If I can get it through that window, I win.

2011
02:17:28,620 --> 02:17:42,720
Ah, it didn't go in.

2012
02:17:42,720 --> 02:17:45,460
It's fine.

2013
02:17:45,460 --> 02:17:49,730
It's fine, it's fine.

2014
02:17:49,730 --> 02:18:03,270
It's fine, totally fine, that just now was totally fine.

2015
02:18:03,270 --> 02:18:05,550
Is it seriously not abandoned?

2016
02:18:05,550 --> 02:18:07,150
This is bad.

2017
02:18:07,150 --> 02:18:10,960
What do I do?

2018
02:18:10,960 --> 02:18:22,320
Oh, can I keep going?

2019
02:18:22,320 --> 02:18:29,910
A horse, huh...

2020
02:18:29,910 --> 02:18:41,920
There was a perfect goal spot right there.

2021
02:18:41,920 --> 02:18:47,360
The colors were just completely different — that was the only issue.

2022
02:18:47,360 --> 02:18:54,210
At least a similar color — at least one of them.

2023
02:18:54,210 --> 02:19:23,590
Should I aim for this one? I want to match one of them.

2024
02:19:23,590 --> 02:19:27,930
I'm going back — can I do a full lap?

2025
02:19:27,930 --> 02:19:49,120
Shadow is definitely the best. Whose house is this?

2026
02:19:49,180 --> 02:19:50,980
Whoa, I've never been to this side before.

2027
02:19:50,980 --> 02:19:52,840
Looks freezing.

2028
02:19:52,840 --> 02:19:54,670
Too cold.

2029
02:19:54,670 --> 02:19:55,470
Okay?

2030
02:19:55,470 --> 02:19:57,430
The horse probably isn't alive here.

2031
02:19:57,430 --> 02:20:04,110
This is a road, right?

2032
02:20:04,110 --> 02:20:07,110
Wait, am I getting shot at? Is this place...

2033
02:20:07,110 --> 02:20:17,800
But it did say it was a road.

2034
02:20:17,800 --> 02:20:31,180
And I'm going outside but I'm getting hit with radiation?

2035
02:20:31,180 --> 02:20:33,180
What's going on? Isn't this place insanely dangerous?

2036
02:20:33,180 --> 02:20:36,280
Hey hey hey hey!

2037
02:20:36,280 --> 02:22:49,410
Hey hey hey hey hey hey hey hey hey hey hey hey hey!

2038
02:22:49,410 --> 02:22:58,240
The sign is deadly but the trees are fine — what's up with that?

2039
02:22:58,240 --> 02:23:03,960
A horse probably can't survive in this cold.

2040
02:23:03,960 --> 02:23:15,580
I'd love to own a horse that can live in this cold.

2041
02:23:15,580 --> 02:23:21,920
That'd be an arctic horse! It's getting dark — this place must be freezing at night, right?

2042
02:23:21,920 --> 02:23:32,380
It's fur! It's fur! Wait, this is a snow country perfume! I need to find shelter somewhere.

2043
02:23:32,380 --> 02:23:38,840
At this rate I'll be buried in snow and die. And it's getting even darker. Melting away, sinking away...

2044
02:23:38,840 --> 02:23:54,660
Gradually, gradually, gradually... It's currently minus 20 degrees. Minus 20 degrees here.

2045
02:23:54,660 --> 02:24:12,750
No horse here — there's nothing at all. It'd have to be a polar bear. If one showed up, that horse would be tough.

2046
02:24:12,750 --> 02:24:26,060
It'd be the strongest alive — well, it's a horse, not a human. Where is it? Where?

2047
02:24:26,060 --> 02:24:28,360
Heave-ho. It's nighttime, huh.

2048
02:24:28,360 --> 02:24:33,520
I want to get through the snowy road before night — get through, get through, GET THROUGH!

2049
02:24:33,520 --> 02:24:36,220
Come on, that's on you. Oh wow.

2050
02:24:36,220 --> 02:24:46,210
An attraction you can enjoy casually.

2051
02:24:46,210 --> 02:24:52,700
Ah, if I came this way I could get close to breaking through.

2052
02:24:52,700 --> 02:24:56,860
But now the trees — WHOA!

2053
02:24:56,860 --> 02:24:59,820
I made it out of the cold zone!

2054
02:24:59,820 --> 02:25:01,820
Whoa, I'm halfway there!

2055
02:25:01,820 --> 02:25:04,720
I want to get back to the garage soon.

2056
02:25:04,720 --> 02:25:10,170
Gas is totally fine though.

2057
02:25:10,170 --> 02:25:17,630
It's cold, so let me cook some meat.

2058
02:25:17,630 --> 02:25:26,230
Oh, turn on the lights!

2059
02:25:26,230 --> 02:25:33,030
Crackling away.

2060
02:25:33,030 --> 02:25:41,280
Ah right, the lights.

2061
02:25:41,280 --> 02:25:42,860
I knew that.

2062
02:25:42,860 --> 02:25:45,500
So there's the horse, the chicken, and...

2063
02:25:45,500 --> 02:25:46,880
They're slightly different.

2064
02:25:46,880 --> 02:25:52,020
I just need to take these three from around here.

2065
02:25:52,020 --> 02:25:54,460
Whoa, something suddenly...

2066
02:25:54,460 --> 02:25:55,840
Even I'm getting sleepy.

2067
02:25:55,840 --> 02:25:56,400
What is this?

2068
02:25:56,400 --> 02:25:59,960
Did I get infected?

2069
02:25:59,960 --> 02:26:01,900
This sleepiness...

2070
02:26:01,900 --> 02:26:02,880
What is it?

2071
02:26:02,880 --> 02:26:10,230
I need to find

2072
02:26:10,230 --> 02:26:12,330
something tasty.

2073
02:26:12,330 --> 02:26:14,110
Let's head to N7.

2074
02:26:14,110 --> 02:26:18,110
And now I suddenly want to eat salmon roe too.

2075
02:26:18,110 --> 02:26:19,590
Incredible.

2076
02:26:19,590 --> 02:26:21,430
All these cravings hitting at once.

2077
02:26:21,430 --> 02:26:26,330
All these cravings hitting at once.

2078
02:26:26,330 --> 02:26:31,860
When humans are in a tough spot

2079
02:26:31,860 --> 02:26:33,380
or pushed to their limits,

2080
02:26:33,380 --> 02:26:34,620
sleepiness suddenly hits.

2081
02:26:34,620 --> 02:26:36,820
Maybe I'm trying to forget everything.

2082
02:26:36,820 --> 02:26:39,220
What is this even, seriously?

2083
02:26:39,220 --> 02:26:51,340
I panicked doing all sorts of things,

2084
02:26:51,340 --> 02:26:54,920
and it all came down to that, huh.

2085
02:26:54,920 --> 02:26:57,860
N7 is so far away though.

2086
02:26:57,860 --> 02:26:58,940
One more time.

2087
02:26:58,940 --> 02:27:02,560
Who's there?

2088
02:27:02,560 --> 02:27:04,740
Hello?

2089
02:27:04,740 --> 02:27:07,080
We're live over here.

2090
02:27:07,080 --> 02:27:09,340
We're live, you know.

2091
02:27:09,340 --> 02:27:12,080
Are you looking for me right now?

2092
02:27:12,080 --> 02:27:14,760
Yes I am!

2093
02:27:14,760 --> 02:27:20,660
Nene, my horse is about to starve to death!

2094
02:27:20,660 --> 02:27:24,400
Wait, why did you let it starve? Is it still okay?

2095
02:27:24,400 --> 02:27:31,720
I couldn't gather enough food, so it's getting exhausted.

2096
02:27:31,720 --> 02:27:38,940
Didn't I tell you to take proper responsibility when you buy one?

2097
02:27:38,940 --> 02:27:45,780
At this rate, Nene's horse is going to starve and disappear before the next login.

2098
02:27:45,780 --> 02:27:49,080
In that case, Zeta will take good care of it.

2099
02:27:49,080 --> 02:27:50,420
That'd be better, right?

2100
02:27:50,420 --> 02:27:54,340
Are you looking for Zeta's horse?

2101
02:27:54,340 --> 02:27:56,000
Huh?

2102
02:27:56,000 --> 02:27:58,260
No no, that's not it.

2103
02:27:58,260 --> 02:28:03,100
That's not it at all.

2104
02:28:03,100 --> 02:28:06,300
Wait, are you guys after Zeta's horse?

2105
02:28:06,300 --> 02:28:09,220
Ah, it was an accident.

2106
02:28:09,220 --> 02:28:12,740
Oh, so that's why you're looking for a horse, Omarun? Is that it?

2107
02:28:12,740 --> 02:28:18,100
The car didn't even break, so— yeah, that's right.

2108
02:28:18,100 --> 02:28:23,060
Before lunch I tuned into Omarun's stream and she was all sweaty,

2109
02:28:23,060 --> 02:28:29,280
and I was like what's going on— turns out she needs a horse. Use the worst horse, Omarun!

2110
02:28:29,280 --> 02:28:34,820
It'll starve to death— before it does, I have to go to her place.

2111
02:28:34,820 --> 02:28:40,480
I have to— I'll hand over the horse, tie it up. This is a matter of life and principle.

2112
02:28:40,480 --> 02:28:46,000
Thank you, I received it— take it, take it!

2113
02:28:46,000 --> 02:28:48,840
Bye bye! I'll give you 1000 Scrapper next time!

2114
02:28:48,840 --> 02:28:54,560
Thank you! Byebye!

2115
02:29:01,130 --> 02:29:05,370
What a good person. You need teammates like that.

2116
02:29:05,370 --> 02:29:08,670
What if it matches up after this?

2117
02:29:08,670 --> 02:29:11,980
Hold on, um...

2118
02:29:11,980 --> 02:29:16,270
Um...

2119
02:29:16,270 --> 02:29:22,810
Calm down, Polka. Calm down, Polka-chan, let's calm down.

2120
02:29:22,810 --> 02:29:27,850
Right. Good girl, good girl.

2121
02:29:27,850 --> 02:29:34,510
I'm taking the horse, so what do I do now?

2122
02:29:34,510 --> 02:29:43,830
I have to bring food too.

2123
02:29:43,830 --> 02:30:03,530
Not Haztold, go up.

2124
02:30:03,530 --> 02:30:07,170
Okay, I'm heading out.

2125
02:30:07,170 --> 02:30:13,230
Calmed down a bit? Yeah I have. Polka did some things she shouldn't have,

2126
02:30:13,230 --> 02:30:15,970
and I was really huffing and puffing just now,

2127
02:30:15,970 --> 02:30:19,850
but man, is that what an offline raid is?

2128
02:30:19,850 --> 02:30:23,270
Polka did some really bad things—

2129
02:30:23,270 --> 02:30:24,290
I did it to Suba-chan too,

2130
02:30:24,290 --> 02:30:28,610
and I'll just have to keep apologizing and making excuses later.

2131
02:30:28,610 --> 02:30:30,710
I'll just have to grovel and keep on living.

2132
02:30:30,710 --> 02:30:33,330
Am I okay? I shouldn't go either.

2133
02:30:33,330 --> 02:30:38,560
Yeah, I guess so.

2134
