Let's light the torches!

2405
02:52:58,580 --> 02:53:00,460
Oh, the birds are chirping.

2406
02:53:00,460 --> 02:53:01,780
So nice.

2407
02:53:01,780 --> 02:53:08,940
Nice, how's everyone doing?

2408
02:53:08,940 --> 02:53:20,920
So Sui-chan runs on C4 instead of gold? I see.

2409
02:53:20,920 --> 02:53:32,430
Let's make two of each.

2410
02:53:32,430 --> 02:53:37,530
With enough energy, you can do anything!

2411
02:53:37,530 --> 02:53:44,150
Alright then— oh, this is a rocket.

2412
02:53:44,150 --> 02:53:47,200
Now then, Pol-chan.

2413
02:53:47,200 --> 02:53:51,890
Can you do it, Pol-chan? Today?

2414
02:53:52,330 --> 02:53:59,950
Can we make it today? Can we do it with a pistol, Pol-chan?

2415
02:53:59,950 --> 02:54:04,290
It's okay, Pol-chan can do it. You've got this.

2416
02:54:04,290 --> 02:54:11,600
Should I bring some cloth? It might be cold, so I'll just take this.

2417
02:54:11,600 --> 02:54:15,160
Pol-chan can do it. Cloth.

2418
02:54:15,160 --> 02:54:26,920
Rather than crafting slowly, let's just make it from raw materials.

2419
02:54:26,920 --> 02:54:32,140
Alright. It's cold, huh.

2420
02:54:32,140 --> 02:54:34,930
Eh, whatever.

2421
02:54:34,930 --> 02:54:44,480
Eating some food and stuff.

2422
02:54:44,480 --> 02:54:58,660
Drinking some water and stuff. Collecting the empty ones and stuff.

2423
02:54:59,040 --> 02:55:01,340
Sitting down and stuff.

2424
02:55:01,340 --> 02:55:08,890
More water too.

2425
02:55:08,890 --> 02:55:15,810
Oh right, you can stack empty bottles together.

2426
02:55:15,810 --> 02:55:19,810
Yeah, stack them— oh, you can stack the water. That's what I meant.

2427
02:55:19,810 --> 02:55:29,050
That hadn't gotten through to Holka.

2428
02:55:29,050 --> 02:55:33,790
Heave-ho.

2429
02:55:33,790 --> 02:55:36,150
Somewhere with firepower… lame?

2430
02:55:36,150 --> 02:55:41,980
Let's see, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5.

2431
02:55:41,980 --> 02:55:43,980
There are 5 in there!

2432
02:55:43,980 --> 02:55:46,770
Nice.

2433
02:55:46,770 --> 02:55:57,450
Ahh~

2434
02:55:57,450 --> 02:56:01,870
Let's eat it right away while it's fresh!

2435
02:56:01,870 --> 02:56:02,790
Fresh out of the oven, fresh out of the oven!

2436
02:56:02,790 --> 02:56:03,690
Delicious, delicious!

2437
02:56:03,690 --> 02:56:14,630
Man, I'm really glad Nene

2438
02:56:14,630 --> 02:56:17,310
came through for me like that.

2439
02:56:18,570 --> 02:56:21,370
I was about to not be able to face Zeta-chan anymore.

2440
02:56:21,370 --> 02:56:25,230
Like, the next time I logged in I'd basically deserve to get shot at forever.

2441
02:56:25,230 --> 02:56:26,730
That was close.

2442
02:56:26,730 --> 02:56:33,300
Teams are the best.

2443
02:56:33,300 --> 02:56:39,850
It really is all about the team.

2444
02:56:39,850 --> 02:56:45,710
I'll definitely apologize to Subaru-san.

2445
02:56:45,710 --> 02:57:15,370
That was seriously bad.

2446
02:57:19,010 --> 02:57:20,470
This is tough.

2447
02:57:20,470 --> 02:57:31,500
I wonder if it's okay to bring it along.

2448
02:57:31,500 --> 02:57:33,520
Well, it should be fine.

2449
02:57:33,520 --> 02:57:41,090
Huh, it got closed.

2450
02:57:41,090 --> 02:57:52,780
This game is seriously hard.

2451
02:57:52,780 --> 02:57:54,640
I can't believe that flag got triggered.

2452
02:57:54,640 --> 02:58:02,610
Alright, alright, alright.

2453
02:58:02,610 --> 02:58:17,110
Departing!

2454
02:58:17,110 --> 02:58:20,540
I'm going on foot.

2455
02:58:20,540 --> 02:58:25,340
It's bright.

2456
02:58:25,340 --> 02:58:43,200
Pretty bright. Pretty morning. Pretty morning? Is it noon?

2457
02:58:43,200 --> 02:58:48,930
Where was it again? Around L11?

2458
02:58:48,930 --> 02:58:52,300
To a cold place~♪

2459
02:58:52,300 --> 02:59:08,070
To a cold place~♪

2460
02:59:08,070 --> 02:59:11,290
Well, it's close.

2461
02:59:11,290 --> 02:59:15,770
It's really close.

2462
02:59:15,770 --> 02:59:20,610
The 15-minute inn is super popular today too.

2463
02:59:20,610 --> 02:59:35,250
That's definitely Sui-chan. 100% Sui-chan.

2464
02:59:35,250 --> 02:59:47,110
Based on the direction too, it's definitely Sui-chan.

2465
02:59:47,110 --> 02:59:49,910
I'm hungry.

2466
02:59:49,910 --> 02:59:56,710
I feel like I haven't eaten dinner. Maybe it's just me.

2467
02:59:56,710 --> 03:00:00,530
We're already inside the territory. Wait, that's weird.

2468
03:00:00,530 --> 03:00:17,650
I'd like them to stay within F and E.

2469
03:00:17,650 --> 03:00:21,340
Oh, I didn't make it in time.

2470
03:00:21,340 --> 03:00:25,530
It was just a regular Psycho Pass.

2471
03:00:25,530 --> 03:00:28,590
10%! 10%! Pull the 10%! The 10%!

2472
03:00:28,590 --> 03:00:31,650
If not now, when will you ever pull the 10%?

2473
03:00:31,650 --> 03:00:33,990
Huh? Who?

2474
03:00:33,990 --> 03:00:36,070
Who's there?

2475
03:00:36,070 --> 03:00:37,670
Who?

2476
03:00:37,670 --> 03:00:40,540
Who is it?

2477
03:00:40,540 --> 03:01:00,840
"Sui-chan!? I have no idea… I have no idea…"

2478
03:01:00,840 --> 03:01:06,420
"Is it trending to knock someone down and then revive them?"

2479
03:01:06,420 --> 03:01:19,400
"Wait, is that the territory… did that leave Sui-chan's territory? Huh? Polka-man still couldn't get out? Is this all Sui-chan's domain?"

2480
03:01:19,400 --> 03:01:23,920
This is bad, I have basically no HP.

2481
03:01:23,920 --> 03:01:36,750
I thought Sui-chan was in her last moments but she's already going at it, she's really going at it

2482
03:01:36,750 --> 03:01:48,930
The way everyone checks who they shot after firing is too funny — no greeting, just gunshots, then exchanging business cards afterward

2483
03:01:49,230 --> 03:01:53,750
Ah, looking for food — but I thought it'd be fine

2484
03:01:53,750 --> 03:02:02,610
Whether she can endure the cold... and then there's Miyauchi's lion

2485
03:02:02,610 --> 03:02:08,330
It's too dark to tell — looked like Miyauchi's lion was coming though

2486
03:02:08,330 --> 03:02:24,410
Wonder what'll happen — should I squeeze in one more sleeping bag?

2487
03:02:24,410 --> 03:02:29,190
Oh, the greeting is no headshot — ah, that's kind of you, at least you're proper about that

2488
03:02:29,430 --> 03:02:33,130
That means you can aim for it

2489
03:02:33,130 --> 03:02:33,930
Intentionally

2490
03:02:33,930 --> 03:02:35,830
Intentionally

2491
03:02:35,830 --> 03:02:39,230
That means you can pull it off

2492
03:02:39,230 --> 03:02:40,330
That's crazy

2493
03:02:40,330 --> 03:02:42,110
The area around the dome is starting to feel ominous too

2494
03:02:42,110 --> 03:02:44,030
Pretty soon

2495
03:02:44,030 --> 03:02:46,720
How on earth are we going to

2496
03:02:46,720 --> 03:02:48,140
everyone

2497
03:02:48,140 --> 03:02:50,100
live a peaceful life from here on

2498
03:02:50,100 --> 03:03:05,370
The moon is rising

2499
03:03:05,370 --> 03:03:08,830
It's hopeless

2500
03:03:08,830 --> 03:03:15,350
There's no peace in the final stretch

2501
03:03:15,350 --> 03:03:23,620
That's exactly right

2502
03:03:23,620 --> 03:03:34,680
Hard to see

2503
03:03:34,680 --> 03:03:38,820
I thought it was around here — maybe a little more this way

2504
03:03:38,820 --> 03:03:53,480
To begin with, 11 is also hollow

2505
03:03:53,480 --> 03:03:59,040
Around here?

2506
03:03:59,040 --> 03:04:01,600
Should I die one more time?

2507
03:04:01,600 --> 03:04:09,180
If anything

2508
03:04:09,180 --> 03:04:11,980
the fact that it's close means

2509
03:04:11,980 --> 03:04:16,340
maybe if I die one more time I can get there?

2510
03:04:16,340 --> 03:04:19,970
My thinking has become

2511
03:04:19,970 --> 03:04:21,050
Re:Zero at this point

2512
03:04:21,050 --> 03:04:21,570
Is this it right now

2513
03:04:21,570 --> 03:04:33,380
Hmm

2514
03:04:33,380 --> 03:04:37,200
No way

2515
03:04:37,200 --> 03:04:43,020
Wait, I'm out of ammo

2516
03:04:43,020 --> 03:04:43,680
Either way

2517
03:04:43,680 --> 03:04:47,620
Hmm

2518
03:04:47,620 --> 03:04:49,200
It was right in front of me though

2519
03:04:49,200 --> 03:04:54,520
And so, finally

2520
03:04:54,520 --> 03:04:57,390
Oh, she came down

2521
03:04:57,390 --> 03:05:01,510
You can't come down

2522
03:05:01,510 --> 03:05:02,870
I don't have the key right now

2523
03:05:02,870 --> 03:05:04,830
Why did you come down

2524
03:05:04,830 --> 03:05:07,310
I'm going with a torch

2525
03:05:07,310 --> 03:05:34,370
The one I just made

2526
03:05:34,370 --> 03:05:34,930
Not at all

2527
03:05:34,930 --> 03:05:37,710
It's in a cold spot, what should I do

2528
03:05:37,710 --> 03:05:43,570
The torch was useless — the flint and steel would've been better

2529
03:05:43,570 --> 03:05:49,070
90 seconds, 20 seconds — where's it coming from

2530
03:05:49,070 --> 03:05:50,430
Is it me

2531
03:05:55,080 --> 03:05:57,740
Once it gets bright, I win

2532
03:05:57,740 --> 03:06:05,780
Within 265 seconds

2533
03:06:05,780 --> 03:06:08,080
I will win

2534
03:06:08,080 --> 03:06:12,290
Nothing happened

2535
03:06:12,290 --> 03:06:16,170
Within these 265 seconds, Polka will

2536
03:06:16,170 --> 03:06:17,550
win

2537
03:06:17,550 --> 03:06:21,920
Didn't have to wait all 265 seconds!

2538
03:06:21,920 --> 03:06:22,920
That's how I'll make it go

2539
03:06:22,920 --> 03:06:39,460
Polka doesn't even need to wait 265 seconds

2540
03:06:39,460 --> 03:06:40,140
She can do it

2541
03:06:40,140 --> 03:06:41,140
Did anyone time it?

2542
03:06:41,580 --> 03:06:44,220
265 seconds

2543
03:06:44,220 --> 03:06:57,840
I'll be done in less than 265 seconds from now

2544
03:06:57,840 --> 03:06:59,500
Of course

2545
03:06:59,500 --> 03:07:05,130
With my fists

2546
03:07:05,130 --> 03:07:06,890
Umbilical cable disconnected?

2547
03:07:06,890 --> 03:07:09,230
Switching to internal inspection?

2548
03:07:09,230 --> 03:07:15,120
So that's what it is

2549
03:07:15,120 --> 03:07:19,170
I'll probably get taken out by the wolf again

2550
03:07:19,170 --> 03:07:20,470
No, the wolf can be ign—

2551
03:07:20,470 --> 03:07:22,270
Wooolf~

2552
03:07:22,270 --> 03:07:25,570
Happy belated birthday, Mio-san

2553
03:07:25,570 --> 03:07:27,290
Let's ignore the wolf

2554
03:07:27,290 --> 03:07:30,030
Ignore, ignore

2555
03:07:30,030 --> 03:07:36,320
Even if it's there, ignore it

2556
03:07:36,320 --> 03:07:37,940
After this long journey

2557
03:07:37,940 --> 03:07:41,100
ending up on Nene's horse

2558
03:07:41,100 --> 03:07:58,930
is very on-brand for this whole adventure

2559
03:07:58,930 --> 03:08:01,390
Now then, we're getting close

2560
03:08:01,390 --> 03:08:08,370
The wolf has probably forgotten we're enemies by now

2561
03:08:08,370 --> 03:08:14,290
The key here is 2 bodies — the first body. The first body.

2562
03:08:14,290 --> 03:08:21,530
I don't need the second body. The important one is the first — probably turned into a backpack.

2563
03:08:21,530 --> 03:08:24,310
That's what I'm thinking.

2564
03:08:24,310 --> 03:08:43,670
I let my guard down the moment I spotted the car, so the direction should be right.

2565
03:08:44,310 --> 03:08:58,720
Or did they come from over there?

2566
03:08:58,720 --> 03:09:04,700
Nope, other way. Loot's flying out.

2567
03:09:04,700 --> 03:09:11,340
Cut through the forest, found this,

2568
03:09:11,340 --> 03:09:15,650
and they're dead.

2569
03:09:15,650 --> 03:09:18,950
Hmm, let's see.

2570
03:09:18,950 --> 03:09:24,080
The original body still hasn't been found. It's around here, right?

2571
03:09:24,080 --> 03:09:38,740
The original body… the second body. Found it. There it is.

2572
03:09:38,740 --> 03:09:42,900
Oh! And this is the first body!

2573
03:09:42,900 --> 03:09:48,170
The original.

2574
03:09:48,170 --> 03:09:53,540
Were you carrying anything? What were you trying to fight back with? A pistol?

2575
03:09:53,540 --> 03:09:58,590
Oh wait, zero bullets, so it's fine. OK! We won!

2576
03:09:58,590 --> 03:10:04,530
This is the second one. Second one had a stone. Nice try, torch.

2577
03:10:04,530 --> 03:10:11,790
Don't give me that look. I'm sorry, okay.

2578
03:10:11,790 --> 03:10:14,510
I'm sorry.

2579
03:10:14,510 --> 03:10:22,720
This is a Rainbow Deluxe Stone.

2580
03:10:22,720 --> 03:10:27,320
Sorry. I'm sorry.

2581
03:10:27,320 --> 03:10:31,820
So anyway, I'm probably the third one,

2582
03:10:31,820 --> 03:10:39,240
Hammer.

2583
03:10:39,240 --> 03:10:41,760
A hammer?

2584
03:10:41,760 --> 03:10:43,560
Mr. Hammer?

2585
03:10:43,560 --> 03:10:45,360
Mr. Hammer?

2586
03:10:45,360 --> 03:10:47,160
Mr. Hammer?

2587
03:10:47,160 --> 03:10:48,960
Shinji?

2588
03:10:48,960 --> 03:10:51,040
Mr. Hammer?

2589
03:10:57,980 --> 03:11:03,920
You can never have too many hammers to craft.

2590
03:11:03,920 --> 03:11:33,970
What was I missing again?

2591
03:11:33,970 --> 03:11:38,550
Open! Oh, I pushed it.

2592
03:11:38,550 --> 03:11:39,550
Open!

2593
03:11:39,550 --> 03:11:42,350
Ah, the long one?

2594
03:11:42,350 --> 03:11:47,150
Well, let me swap all of these out for wood ones.

2595
03:11:47,150 --> 03:11:48,950
I'm a bit worried.

2596
03:11:48,950 --> 03:11:53,430
There, perfect.

2597
03:11:54,430 --> 03:11:58,630
Oh, it hasn't weathered that much.

2598
03:11:58,630 --> 03:12:00,430
Good, good.

2599
03:12:00,430 --> 03:12:03,490
Close it up.

2600
03:12:03,490 --> 03:12:10,060
Hmm, and then.

2601
03:12:10,060 --> 03:12:13,830
Put a spare in too.

2602
03:12:13,830 --> 03:12:16,430
Is that perfect?

2603
03:12:16,430 --> 03:12:18,430
Cell phone — let me keep that on me.

2604
03:12:18,430 --> 03:12:23,230
Uh, I'll deal with this one later.

2605
03:12:23,230 --> 03:12:28,790
Phew, half a sheet.

2606
03:12:29,890 --> 03:12:30,890
Time to head back.

2607
03:12:30,890 --> 03:12:34,060
I'm hungry, Poruka-chan.

2608
03:12:34,060 --> 03:12:36,200
Poruka-chan, I'm starving.

2609
03:12:36,200 --> 03:12:44,680
Alright.

2610
03:12:44,680 --> 03:13:12,430
Home sweet home, home sweet home.

2611
03:13:12,430 --> 03:13:16,190
I want to get onto this road first.

2612
03:13:16,190 --> 03:13:21,370
Home sweet home, home sweet home.

2613
03:13:21,370 --> 03:13:51,730
That narrow path — is that even a road?

2614
03:13:51,730 --> 03:13:53,050
Is it a road?

2615
03:13:53,050 --> 03:13:56,780
That's really far away.

2616
03:13:57,120 --> 03:13:58,920
It's really far away.

2617
03:13:58,920 --> 03:14:00,720
Supply drop incoming.

2618
03:14:00,720 --> 03:14:02,520
It's getting farther and farther away.

2619
03:14:02,520 --> 03:14:04,320
Drifting away, drifting away.

2620
03:14:04,320 --> 03:14:06,320
Is it just unpaved?

2621
03:14:06,320 --> 03:14:08,120
Ohhhhh!

2622
03:14:08,120 --> 03:14:10,090
Yeah yeah yeah yeah!

2623
03:14:10,090 --> 03:14:14,870
Oh!

2624
03:14:14,870 --> 03:14:16,870
Knock those trees down too.

2625
03:14:16,870 --> 03:14:18,670
Yeah, go for those trees.

2626
03:14:18,670 --> 03:14:20,470
Still probably—

2627
03:14:20,470 --> 03:14:22,070
Mmph.

2628
03:14:22,070 --> 03:14:24,070
Strong.

2629
03:14:24,070 --> 03:14:25,980
It's a bit strong.

2630
03:14:32,500 --> 03:14:35,480
Uh oh. Should I enter the territory, this Marb?

2631
03:14:35,480 --> 03:14:38,540
Oh, looks like it's leaving the territory.

2632
03:14:38,540 --> 03:14:52,440
Let's go up to here.

2633
03:14:52,440 --> 03:14:54,360
Oh, nicely dodged.

2634
03:14:54,360 --> 03:15:03,720
No, that was my bad.

2635
03:15:03,720 --> 03:15:07,480
Won't it drop here? If that was a supply helicopter just now.

2636
03:15:07,480 --> 03:15:12,600
What do you think?

2637
03:15:12,600 --> 03:15:16,450
Isn't that a supply helicopter?

2638
03:15:16,450 --> 03:15:18,410
What do you reckon?

2639
03:15:18,410 --> 03:15:33,030
Where's the road?

2640
03:15:33,030 --> 03:16:00,620
Uh oh, the dome just turned into a super hot zone.

2641
03:16:00,620 --> 03:16:05,140
The dome's cheap right now,

2642
03:16:05,140 --> 03:16:12,270
because someone with absolutely broken stats just showed up.

2643
03:16:12,270 --> 03:16:18,640
We might even have to move the garage location.

2644
03:16:18,640 --> 03:16:34,200
No territory right now?

2645
03:16:34,200 --> 03:16:35,380
This is bad.

2646
03:16:35,380 --> 03:16:39,860
There are already crazy people here, and more crazy people too.

2647
03:16:39,860 --> 03:16:41,860
And on top of that, there's an even crazier one.

2648
03:16:41,860 --> 03:16:45,620
Why is it only insane people here, seriously?

2649
03:16:45,620 --> 03:16:47,310
Oh, I see them.

2650
03:16:47,310 --> 03:16:50,110
I'd be scared if they're waiting for me, but it should be fine.

2651
03:16:50,110 --> 03:16:53,060
Come on, seriously — what the heck!?

2652
03:16:53,060 --> 03:17:02,690
Is there anything good around here?

2653
03:17:02,690 --> 03:17:06,330
Ahh...

2654
03:17:06,330 --> 03:17:17,680
Are you not going in with a push today?

2655
03:17:17,680 --> 03:17:20,480
It's not that driving is a hassle.

2656
03:17:20,480 --> 03:17:23,280
Push, push push!

2657
03:17:23,280 --> 03:17:23,880
Hm?

2658
03:17:23,880 --> 03:17:38,090
Come on, squeeze in, squeeze in — this way?

2659
03:17:38,090 --> 03:17:58,270
Getting in there was pretty exhausting, dealing with people like that.

2660
03:17:58,270 --> 03:18:03,770
Only the spring's left.

2661
03:18:03,770 --> 03:18:08,650
Trade it for junk.

2662
03:18:08,650 --> 03:18:17,220
Something like this, I guess.

2663
03:18:17,220 --> 03:18:19,980
Nicely tidied up.

2664
03:18:19,980 --> 03:18:25,570
Syringe.

2665
03:18:25,570 --> 03:18:31,530
That'll last 5 days, right?

2666
03:18:31,530 --> 03:18:36,690
Adding more doesn't seem like it'd change much.

2667
03:18:36,690 --> 03:18:41,010
I'll just take this much.

2668
03:18:41,010 --> 03:18:43,370
The rest goes into storage.

2669
03:18:43,370 --> 03:18:45,350
Perfect! Oh yeah!

2670
03:18:45,350 --> 03:18:49,740
It's 6 days now!

2671
03:18:49,740 --> 03:18:51,620
Ugh, I got on again by accident.

2672
03:18:51,620 --> 03:18:56,340
Just making sure I haven't forgotten anything.

2673
03:18:56,340 --> 03:19:00,100
Uh, syringes and stuff...

2674
03:19:00,100 --> 03:19:02,700
Clothes and stuff...

2675
03:19:02,700 --> 03:19:20,880
Everything's been perfect so far — and it'll stay perfect from here too.

2676
03:19:20,880 --> 03:19:25,000
And the spare and the hammer...

2677
03:19:25,000 --> 03:19:29,700
Maybe I'll just take this much back. In that case...

2678
03:19:29,700 --> 03:19:34,420
I'll leave the shotgun ammo here.

2679
03:19:34,420 --> 03:19:37,100
Don't need this.

2680
03:19:40,500 --> 03:19:43,530
Okay, so then...

2681
03:19:43,530 --> 03:19:48,570
I'd like to end today's stream in front of the confessional.

2682
03:19:48,570 --> 03:19:51,890
I am truly, deeply sorry!

2683
03:19:51,890 --> 03:19:57,060
Now I'm off to apologize behind the scenes.

2684
03:19:57,060 --> 03:20:00,520
And thank you to everyone who watched!

2685
03:20:00,520 --> 03:20:05,740
Haah... I just want to lie down in bed right now.

2686
03:20:05,740 --> 03:20:09,520
I need to lie down immediately and just go "ughhh."

2687
03:20:09,520 --> 03:20:19,250
I don't even know who to apologize to or where to start anymore.

2688
03:20:19,250 --> 03:20:22,690
I might come back full of lead bullets.

2689
03:20:22,690 --> 03:20:30,690
Alright, thank you so much — today was really something else.

2690
03:20:30,690 --> 03:20:33,410
Things were already a mess before the stream even started.

2691
03:20:33,410 --> 03:20:36,870
Okay, off to Discord!

2692
03:20:36,870 --> 03:20:38,030
Here I go!

2693
03:20:38,030 --> 03:20:39,650
Alright everyone, good work today!

2694
03:20:39,650 --> 03:20:42,590
Starting at 1 today —

2695
03:20:42,590 --> 03:20:44,510
Flarepol Roadshow!

2696
03:20:44,510 --> 03:20:45,910
Since I removed the wave filter,

2697
03:20:45,910 --> 03:20:47,510
the old scenes —

2698
03:20:47,510 --> 03:20:50,210
we're watching the Evangelion movie, so please check that out too!

2699
03:20:50,210 --> 03:20:51,410
It's Flare's stream!

2700
03:20:51,410 --> 03:20:52,230
Well then —

2701
03:20:52,230 --> 03:20:54,730
Good work everyone, otsu-pol, oyasumi-pol!

2702
03:20:54,730 --> 03:20:56,270
Goodnight-pol!

2703
03:20:56,270 --> 03:20:57,730
Pol pol!

2704
03:20:57,730 --> 03:21:06,320
When all is said and done,

2705
03:21:06,320 --> 03:21:08,740
it was fun.
